    {"id": "MARKET-ChalhoubGroup_Unders-006", "title": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without", "content": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without AuthorizationWhat Role Does Fashion\nPlay in Saudis ’ Lives? \nChalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without Authorization\n\nChalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without AuthorizationFashion is… a key area of spending \n79%\nranked retail shopping in their\ntop 3 areas of discretionary spending\n48%\nfor dining out 41%\nfor electronics vs. AFFLUENT\nWOMEN\nSECONDARY CITIES\nREMOTE CITIES\nWhen it comes to your disposable income, please rank your top three a", "source": "market/ChalhoubGroup-Understanding-the-Modern-KSA-Fashion-Consumer_for_partners.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-ChalhoubGroup_Unders-007", "title": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without", "content": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without AuthorizationFashion is… first and foremost a means of expression \n70% “A way of expressing my personality and style”\n60% “A way of rewarding myself”\n56% “A way of standing out from the crowd”\n50% \n“A way of showing my \nsocial status” PRIMARY CITIES\n38% \n“A way of connecting \nwith my peers” Secondary cities Remote cities \nvs 45% \nin primary cities  vs30%\nin primary cities When it comes to your relationship with fashion, which of the below statements do you \nrelate to the most? Please rank up to three statements th", "source": "market/ChalhoubGroup-Understanding-the-Modern-KSA-Fashion-Consumer_for_partners.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-ChalhoubGroup_Unders-008", "title": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without", "content": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without Authorization\nFashion is… about comfort and recognition  \nPRIMARY CITIES61% Wear pieces from recognizable brands\n60% Wear comfortable and practical pieces\n53% Wear the latest fashion trends\nREMOTE CITIES: LESS TREND DRIVEN \n50%\nWear pieces from \nrecognisable brands 45%\nWear the latest \nfashion trends54%\nWear unique pieces \nno-one else will haveSECONDARY CITIES\nWhen it comes to your fashion style, which of the below statements best describe your style?\nPlease rank up to three of the statements that best describe th", "source": "market/ChalhoubGroup-Understanding-the-Modern-KSA-Fashion-Consumer_for_partners.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-ChalhoubGroup_Unders-009", "title": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without", "content": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without AuthorizationPrimary cities pushing demand for athleisure \n53%* plan on buying activewear in the coming 12 months 85%* in primary cities plan on buying sneakers in the coming 12 months \n*Among those who plan on buying shoes/clothes in the \ncoming 12 months vs 48% in remote cities\nvs 38% in remote cities\nYou mentioned you’re likely to buy clothes /shoes in the next 12 months. \nWhat kind of clothes/shoes are you most likely to buy?", "source": "market/ChalhoubGroup-Understanding-the-Modern-KSA-Fashion-Consumer_for_partners.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-ChalhoubGroup_Unders-010", "title": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without", "content": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without AuthorizationWhile remote cities push traditional clothing and footwear \n64%* plan on buying sandals in the coming 12 months 45% in remote cities plan on buying traditional clothing in the coming 12 months \n*Among those who plan on buying \nshoes in the coming 12 months vs 22% in primary cities\nvs 42% in primary cities\nIn the next 12 months, which of the below categories are you most likely to buy? \nPlease rank up to three categories", "source": "market/ChalhoubGroup-Understanding-the-Modern-KSA-Fashion-Consumer_for_partners.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-ChalhoubGroup_Unders-011", "title": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without", "content": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without Authorization\nFashion is… still mostly about mainstream brands\nbut primary and secondary cities pushing beyond this  \nPRIMARY CITIES 69% Buy from well -known, international brands\n58% Buy from niche brands\n52% Buy from sustainable brands\nREMOTE CITIES: LOCAL DESIGNERS BUT NOT QUITE AS WE KNOW IT \n61%\nBuy from local/regional \nbrands and designers SECONDARY CITIES\nWhen it comes to your purchase behaviour, which of the below statements best describe \nyour behaviour? Please rank up to three of the statements that best", "source": "market/ChalhoubGroup-Understanding-the-Modern-KSA-Fashion-Consumer_for_partners.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-ChalhoubGroup_Unders-012", "title": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without", "content": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without AuthorizationMapping the \nConsumer Journey \nChalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without Authorization\n\nChalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without AuthorizationFashion inspiration typically starts online... \nless so in remote cities  \n42% Instagram\n29% Browsing online  \n29% YouTube\n28% Browsing the mall  \n25% Family & friends REMOTE CITIESREMOTE CITIES\nWhere do you get your fashion inspiration from? Please select up to \nthree answers", "source": "market/ChalhoubGroup-Understanding-the-Modern-KSA-Fashion-Consumer_for_partners.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-ChalhoubGroup_Unders-013", "title": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without", "content": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without AuthorizationA lower proportion of Saudis in remote cities buy above fast fashion \nvs~29% ~3%~44% <SAR 30,000\nof Saudis in remote cities \ndon’t buy premium, affordable luxury \nor high end luxury  fashionof Saudis in primary or secondary cities \ndon’t buy premium, affordable luxury\nor high end luxury  fashion\nWhen shopping for fashion brands, do you usually shop in -store or \nonline? (Those who answered “I do not buy this category”", "source": "market/ChalhoubGroup-Understanding-the-Modern-KSA-Fashion-Consumer_for_partners.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-ChalhoubGroup_Unders-014", "title": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without", "content": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without AuthorizationSaudis are omnichannel shoppers…\nbut more fast fashion is bought in -store \n20%\nin-store only 4%\nonline only 69%\nboth\n+ fast fashion\n+ males; lower middle \nclass \nWhen shopping for fashion brands, do you usually shop in -store or \nonline?\n\nChalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without AuthorizationWhether online or in -store, Saudis tend to shop most often from the brand itself \n#1 Brand store \n#2 Department store \n#3 Concept store \n#4 Seasonal pop -up\n#5 Outlet stor", "source": "market/ChalhoubGroup-Understanding-the-Modern-KSA-Fashion-Consumer_for_partners.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-ChalhoubGroup_Unders-015", "title": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without", "content": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without Authorization\nOnline Deep -Dive\n\nChalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without AuthorizationOnline shopping is primarily about convenience \nConvenience 31%\nSafety (lower COVID risk) 29%\nBrand variety 28%\nBrowse without \npressure to buy  26%More offers 24%\nBetter prices  23%\nBrand not found\nin my city 23%\nREMOTE CITIESPRIMARY CITIES\nREMOTE CITIES\nYou mentioned you also shop fashion online. What are your main reasons \nfor shopping fashion online? Please select up to three main reas", "source": "market/ChalhoubGroup-Understanding-the-Modern-KSA-Fashion-Consumer_for_partners.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-ChalhoubGroup_Unders-016", "title": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without", "content": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without AuthorizationAlthough Saudis still turn to international sites for fashion\n28%\nInt’l sites only 2%\nlocal sites only 70%\nboth\n+ fast & premium fashion  \nWhen shopping for fashion online, which of the below statements best \ndescribe your behaviour?\n\nChalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without AuthorizationAs they look for variety, limited editions and better prices \n22%35%37%41%43%45%47%\nPay in installmentsQuick deliveryBrand not in KSAPricesProduct varietyLimited editionsBrand v", "source": "market/ChalhoubGroup-Understanding-the-Modern-KSA-Fashion-Consumer_for_partners.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-ChalhoubGroup_Unders-017", "title": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without", "content": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without Authorization(Inter) national \nTravel \nChalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without Authorization\n\nChalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without AuthorizationDomestic travel is an opportunity when it comes to developing retail in KSA \n35%\nin city only4%\nother cities only61%\nboth\n+ fast fashion + remote cities \n+ primary cities + luxury fashion\nWhich of the below best describes your behaviour when shopping in -store \nfor fashion", "source": "market/ChalhoubGroup-Understanding-the-Modern-KSA-Fashion-Consumer_for_partners.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-ChalhoubGroup_Unders-018", "title": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without", "content": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without AuthorizationAttractiveness of seasonal pop -ups… especially Riyadh Season \n8%26%26%28%33%41%42%66%\nI won\'t be attending any major eventsMDL BeastWinter at TantoraFormula 1Riyadh OasisDiriyah SeasonJanadriya SeasonRiyadh Season\nWhich of the below upcoming events are you most likely to attend ?\n\nChalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without Authorization40%50%52%53%65%65%\nSporting eventsExhibitionsMusical concertsFood and diningFamily entertainmentShopping\nAppeal of Riyadh Season ", "source": "market/ChalhoubGroup-Understanding-the-Modern-KSA-Fashion-Consumer_for_partners.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-ChalhoubGroup_Unders-019", "title": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without", "content": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without Authorization\"I prefer shopping in London, where I spend my time shopping in \ndepartment stores and high streets. I like the experience of walking \naround, trying things on and sitting down for a coffee between\"On shopping abroad: \nInsights from qualitative interviews", "source": "market/ChalhoubGroup-Understanding-the-Modern-KSA-Fashion-Consumer_for_partners.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-ChalhoubGroup_Unders-020", "title": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without", "content": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without AuthorizationMajority plan on travelling abroad, with a preference for Dubai \n68% \nDubai39% \nParis36% \nLondon68% \nYes15% \nMaybe17%\nNo\nAFFLUENT REMOTE CITIES\nNow that the borders are opening, do you plan on travelling abroad for shopping in the next six months? *border opening pushed following the launch of fieldwork* \nWhat would be your preferred shopping destinations abroad? Please rank up to three of your top choices\nPRIMARY CITIES\nChalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without ", "source": "market/ChalhoubGroup-Understanding-the-Modern-KSA-Fashion-Consumer_for_partners.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-ChalhoubGroup_Unders-021", "title": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without", "content": "Chalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without AuthorizationDriven by variety and exclusivity, but also the wider shopping experience \n45%    Brand variety  \n41%    Product variety \n39%    Exclusive items \n34%    Shop outdoorsAtmosphere    33%  Lower prices    24%  Customer service    23%  \nPRIMARY CITIES\nPRIMARY CITIES\nWhy do you prefer shopping abroad instead of in Saudi Arabia?\n\nChalhoub Group @ Copyright 2021 Strictly Confidential –Do Not Distribute Without Authorization\nUnderstanding\nthe Modern Saudi\nFashion Consumer\nThank you", "source": "market/ChalhoubGroup-Understanding-the-Modern-KSA-Fashion-Consumer_for_partners.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Cross_Cultural_Aesth-001", "title": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama,  Sosial dan Budaya  ", "content": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama,  Sosial dan Budaya  \nhttps://journal.iaimnumetrolampung.ac.id/index.php/jf   \n \nFikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan Budaya  \nDOI: https://doi.org/ 10.25217/jf.v10i1.5527     \nCross -Cultural Aesthetics: Integrating Abaya  and K -Fashion in \nContemporary Muslim Fashion Design  \n \nNabilah Tsuroya Basya* , Ahmad Ashfia \nUniversitas Islam Negeri Sunan  Kalijaga  Yogyakarta , Indonesia  \nUniversitas Islam Negeri  Syarif Hidayatullah  Jakarta , Indonesia  \n*Correspondence :  natsubasy@gmail.com   \n \nAbstra ct  \nAcculturation in fashion arises as a result of globalizati", "source": "market/Cross-Cultural Aesthetics Integrating Abaya and K-Fashion in.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Cross_Cultural_Aesth-002", "title": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  ", "content": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  \nVolume 10, Number 1, June 202 5 Nabilah Tsuroya Basya, Ahmad Ashfia  \nCross -Cultural Aesthetics … \n     \n191 \n fashionable piety, but also positions social media as a new authoritative space in determining the \nvisual identity of contemporary Muslim women (2024c ).  \nThis phenomenon shows the increasingly strong position of th e Muslim fashion industry in \nIndonesia, which now acts not only as a consumption product but also as a form of cultural \nexpression and belief  (Syadiyah et al., 2024 ). Driven by global influence through social media an", "source": "market/Cross-Cultural Aesthetics Integrating Abaya and K-Fashion in.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Cross_Cultural_Aesth-003", "title": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  ", "content": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  \nVolume 10, Number 1, June 202 5 Nabilah Tsuroya Basya, Ahmad Ashfia  \nCross -Cultural Aesthetics … \n     \n192 \n such as abaya , makes a style that is more modern, stylish, and close to international trends that are \nalso accepted by the younger generation.  \nA comprehensive search of the academic literature on cultural acculturation shows that a \nvariety of studies have been conduct ed. However, there is still a significant research gap, namely \nthe absence of in -depth studies that explore the expression of Islamic identity through the medium \n", "source": "market/Cross-Cultural Aesthetics Integrating Abaya and K-Fashion in.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Cross_Cultural_Aesth-004", "title": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  ", "content": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  \nVolume 10, Number 1, June 202 5 Nabilah Tsuroya Basya, Ahmad Ashfia  \nCross -Cultural Aesthetics … \n     \n193 \n 2006 ). Based on the data collected from both abaya  and K -fashion informants, the research results \nwill be described based on modeling theory, as follows:  \n \nAttention  \nThe Attention component includes questions that focus on the reasons why abaya  attracts \nattention and is an attraction for its users. From the results of the interview on November 20, 2024, \nboth informants said that interest in abaya  arose becau se of the trans", "source": "market/Cross-Cultural Aesthetics Integrating Abaya and K-Fashion in.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Cross_Cultural_Aesth-005", "title": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  ", "content": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  \nVolume 10, Number 1, June 202 5 Nabilah Tsuroya Basya, Ahmad Ashfia  \nCross -Cultural Aesthetics … \n     \n194 \n The K -fashion informant answered as follows : \n \nI started to find out about Korean fashion either on a page that discusses fashion or e -commerce \nthat I can, suitable and safe to wear ( Informant, 2024 ). \n \nBuying dupe K -fashion in e -commerce or offline stores at a much more affordable price \n(Informant 4, 2024 ). \n \nFrom all inform ants, it can be seen that through visualization, they can well remember the \npreferred clothing mo", "source": "market/Cross-Cultural Aesthetics Integrating Abaya and K-Fashion in.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Cross_Cultural_Aesth-006", "title": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  ", "content": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  \nVolume 10, Number 1, June 202 5 Nabilah Tsuroya Basya, Ahmad Ashfia  \nCross -Cultural Aesthetics … \n     \n195 \n Motivation  \nMotivation in this case includes the encouragement or reasons for informants to imitate the \nabaya  worn by the model so that they are motivated to wear this fashion. The following are the \ninterview results from the informants : \n \nI wear abaya  because it is suitable, comfortable and suits my body shape. Abaya  gives the \nimpression of being fashionable and polite, which is in accordance with the self -image I want to \ns", "source": "market/Cross-Cultural Aesthetics Integrating Abaya and K-Fashion in.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Cross_Cultural_Aesth-007", "title": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  ", "content": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  \nVolume 10, Number 1, June 202 5 Nabilah Tsuroya Basya, Ahmad Ashfia  \nCross -Cultural Aesthetics … \n     \n196 \n trade, migration, or the exchange of ideas  (Muasmara & Ajmain, 2020 ). Another relevant research \nthat Noorhaidi Hasan in his article said that Muslim teenagers face a complex adaptation process, \nintegrating modernity with Islamic traditions. They adopt fashionable hijab  styles, utilize social \nmedia to share experiences, and actively adapt global culture to the local context. This forms a \nhybrid identity that combines religious va", "source": "market/Cross-Cultural Aesthetics Integrating Abaya and K-Fashion in.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Cross_Cultural_Aesth-008", "title": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  ", "content": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  \nVolume 10, Number 1, June 202 5 Nabilah Tsuroya Basya, Ahmad Ashfia  \nCross -Cultural Aesthetics … \n     \n197 \n diverse facilities offered ranging from social networks, videos, photos, news, or even other needs \nsuch as clothing that can be found through internet access and obtained easily. This convenience has \nresulted in the fulfillment of increased consumption of fashion  (Diwanti & Budiyati, 2023 ). \nGlobalization also provides wider access to fashion trends from around the world through social \nmedia and digital platforms. Globalization al", "source": "market/Cross-Cultural Aesthetics Integrating Abaya and K-Fashion in.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Cross_Cultural_Aesth-009", "title": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  ", "content": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  \nVolume 10, Number 1, June 202 5 Nabilah Tsuroya Basya, Ahmad Ashfia  \nCross -Cultural Aesthetics … \n     \n198 \n fashions in 2024, the abaya  combines classic style, comfort, and elegance, making it a top choice in \nMuslim fashion. (Oliviane Nuah, 2024 ). The transformation of the abaya  from the traditional all -\nblack design to a modern model with varied materials, motifs, and accessories reflects the change in \nthe lifestyle of Muslim women who need flexible clothing. With a design that prioritizes modesty as \nwell as style, modern abaya  come", "source": "market/Cross-Cultural Aesthetics Integrating Abaya and K-Fashion in.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Cross_Cultural_Aesth-010", "title": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  ", "content": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  \nVolume 10, Number 1, June 202 5 Nabilah Tsuroya Basya, Ahmad Ashfia  \nCross -Cultural Aesthetics … \n     \n199 \n designs, comfortable yet stylish sneaker s, and other Korean trinkets complement the overall \naesthetic. With this mix, teens manage to create a modern look that reflects their unique identity, \nwhile showing how global trends can be adapted into local culture  (2024a ). \nK-fashion modification among Indonesian teens encourages creativity and introduces new \nstyles, but it also has negative impacts. Some teens tend to ignore local cult", "source": "market/Cross-Cultural Aesthetics Integrating Abaya and K-Fashion in.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Cross_Cultural_Aesth-011", "title": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  ", "content": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  \nVolume 10, Number 1, June 202 5 Nabilah Tsuroya Basya, Ahmad Ashfia  \nCross -Cultural Aesthetics … \n     \n200 \n Negative Response to Global Fashion Trends  \nThe adaptation and modification of abaya  and K -fashion has had various impacts, not only \npositive, but also negative impacts that must be addressed in a balanced manner. Cultural \nglobalization encourages the adoption of foreign dressing styles that often i gnore local cultural \nvalues, threatening Indonesia\'s cultural identity. The pressure to follow trends creates a fear of \nbeing left ", "source": "market/Cross-Cultural Aesthetics Integrating Abaya and K-Fashion in.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Cross_Cultural_Aesth-012", "title": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  ", "content": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  \nVolume 10, Number 1, June 202 5 Nabilah Tsuroya Basya, Ahmad Ashfia  \nCross -Cultural Aesthetics … \n     \n201 \n Islamic principles, there exists a risk of diminishing Indonesia\'s cultural identity when global \ninfluences predominate. In certain instances, the reliance on international trends can precipitate a \ncultural identity crisis for adolescents caught between modernity and tradition.  Consequently, a \ncritical approach is essential when selecting fashion trends, including the implementation of \neducational initiatives aimed at managing the", "source": "market/Cross-Cultural Aesthetics Integrating Abaya and K-Fashion in.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Cross_Cultural_Aesth-013", "title": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  ", "content": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  \nVolume 10, Number 1, June 202 5 Nabilah Tsuroya Basya, Ahmad Ashfia  \nCross -Cultural Aesthetics … \n     \n202 \n Immanuel, G., & Pannindriya, S. T. (2020). Dampak Globalisasi Terhadap Gaya Berpakaian \nGenerasi Z Bali. COMMENTATE: Journal of Communication Management , 1(2), 162. \nhttps://doi.org/10.37535/103001220204   \nInouiprint. (2024, March 28). 5 Model Abaya Modern untuk Inspirasi Pebisnis Busana Muslim . \nTextile Digital Printing. Google  \nJanmohamed, S. (2017). Generation M . Bentang. Google  \nJannah, S. R., Khoirunnisa, Z., & Faristiana, A", "source": "market/Cross-Cultural Aesthetics Integrating Abaya and K-Fashion in.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Cross_Cultural_Aesth-014", "title": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  ", "content": "Fikri: Jurnal Kajian Agama, Sosial dan  Budaya  \nVolume 10, Number 1, June 202 5 Nabilah Tsuroya Basya, Ahmad Ashfia  \nCross -Cultural Aesthetics … \n     \n203 \n Rohman, M. F., & Ulinnuha, R. (2022). Halal Influencers: A Representation Of The Trend Of \nHalal -Food Consumption Among The Indonesian Muslim Middle Cla ss. Jurnal Sosiologi \nReflektif , 17(1), 179 –204. https://doi.org/10.14421/jsr.v17i1.2554   \nSari, N. S. (2015). Praktik Sosial Pola Berpakaian Pengguna Korean Style di Surabaya . 03(03).  \nGoogle  \nSilaturrohmah, F., Masruroh, N., & Dzulkarnaen, A. (2024). Islam’s View On Changes In", "source": "market/Cross-Cultural Aesthetics Integrating Abaya and K-Fashion in.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-D1_Coverage_Complian-001", "title": "Coverage & Compliance-Oriented Fit Preferences (D1)", "content": "Coverage & Compliance-Oriented Fit Preferences (D1)\n\nText corpus: compliant description phrasing for length, looseness, opacity/lining, and exposure boundaries (slits/cuffs/hemlines).\n\nAnkle-length / covers the ankles.\n\nFull length, reaching the ankles with a clean hemline.\n\nFloor-length drape for occasion wear.\n\nSkims the floor without dragging.\n\nLong enough for full coverage when walking and sitting.\n\nExtra length to maintain coverage with heels.\n\nHem designed to avoid tripping while keeping full coverage.\n\nModest length that stays ankle-to-floor depending on height.\n\nLoose fit / relaxed fit", "source": "market/D1_Coverage_Compliance_Structural_Preferences_TextCorpus.docx", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-D1_Coverage_Complian-002", "title": "Straight cut / flowing cut that doesn’t outline the body.", "content": "Straight cut / flowing cut that doesn’t outline the body.\n\nBreathable volume for hot weather and movement.\n\nDesigned for full range of motion without pulling.\n\nFully lined for opacity and confidence.\n\nDouble-layered to prevent sheerness in light colors.\n\nChiffon outer with a full lining for full coverage.\n\nNon-sheer fabric with a clean, modest finish.\n\nLining added where needed to avoid transparency under sunlight.\n\nLightweight yet opaque (coverage without heaviness).\n\nModest slit height (limited opening).\n\nSide slits designed for movement without exposure.\n\nSleeves stay in place and maintain ", "source": "market/D1_Coverage_Compliance_Structural_Preferences_TextCorpus.docx", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-D1_Coverage_Complian-003", "title": "Secure closures to prevent accidental exposure.", "content": "Secure closures to prevent accidental exposure.\n\nFull coverage, ankle-length, and opaque with a relaxed, non-cling fit.\n\nLoose, flowy silhouette with full lining to ensure it is not see-through.\n\nAnkle-to-floor length with modest slit placement for movement without exposure.\n\nLightweight chiffon outer, fully lined for opacity, with sleeves that stay in place.\n\nRelaxed shoulders and sleeves, non-sheer fabric, and secure closures for all-day coverage.\n\nModest fashion elements: loose, non-transparent, long sleeves/ankle length: https://modefywear.com/blogs/news/modest-dressing-rules\n\nAbaya length", "source": "market/D1_Coverage_Compliance_Structural_Preferences_TextCorpus.docx", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-D1_Coverage_Complian-004", "title": "Opaque chiffon hijab product language: https://covermecutee.com/products/opaque-", "content": "Opaque chiffon hijab product language: https://covermecutee.com/products/opaque-chiffon-hijabs", "source": "market/D1_Coverage_Compliance_Structural_Preferences_TextCorpus.docx", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-D2_Functional_Struct-001", "title": "Functional Structure Preferences (D2)", "content": "Functional Structure Preferences (D2)\n\nText corpus format: feature → scenario → conversion copy.\n\n功能点：前开拉链（neck / full front zip）\n\n对应场景：晨间赶时间、通勤出门、需要快速穿脱；或希望穿着更“利落”的用户。\n\n转化话术：一拉即合，出门不耽误；拉链隐藏在门襟内，外观依旧干净端庄。\n\n对应场景：带娃、拎包、需要单手操作；或想要开襟叠穿但又担心走动敞开。\n\n转化话术：暗扣一按就稳，开合更省力；门襟内侧加挡片，走动也更安心不露内搭。\n\n功能点：袖口暗扣 / 可开袖（snap-button cuffs）\n\n对应场景：做家务、洗手、吃饭、工作时需要撸袖；但又不想袖口松垮影响外观。\n\n转化话术：袖口可开合，抬手不束缚；需要时固定住袖口，整天保持利落不拖沓。\n\n对应场景：同一件希望覆盖“日常穿闭合”与“外搭叠穿”两种需求。\n\n转化话术：一件两穿：闭合时端庄、外搭时更时髦；省下一套搭配成本。\n\n对应场景：日常外出、商场、接送孩子、通勤；想随手放手机钥匙又不想一直拿包。\n\n转化话术：手机钥匙随手放，解放双手；口袋隐形不鼓包，整体仍然平整有型。\n\n对应场景：人多场景（集市/商场/旅行）、需要更强安全感，担心掉落。\n\n转化话术：口袋带安全结构，走路不担心掉；重要小物贴身收好更放", "source": "market/D2_Functional_Structure_Preferences_TextCorpus.docx", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-D2_Functional_Struct-002", "title": "功能点：多穿法结构（open / closed / belted）", "content": "功能点：多穿法结构（open / closed / belted）\n\n转化话术：三种穿法一件搞定：外搭更轻松、闭合更端庄、系带更显比例。\n\n功能点：内置抽绳腰（adjustable drawstring waist）\n\n对应场景：不同身形/不同体型阶段（体重波动、孕期/产后）；或想在“宽松端庄”和“显比例”间切换。\n\n转化话术：想宽松就放松，想显比例就轻收；一件适配更多身形与状态。\n\n功能点：可调节腰带（detachable / adjustable belt）\n\n对应场景：通勤想更利落、拍照想更显腿长；不同场合需要不同廓形。\n\n转化话术：腰带一系立刻有比例；同款从“慵懒”切到“精致”，变化很明显。\n\n转化话术：隐形调节更干净，正面不破坏端庄线条；坐下起身也更舒适。\n\neasy to wear / easy on-off / quick change\n\nhands-free / pockets for phone & keys\n\ndetachable shawl / removable cape\n\nmultiway styling / multiple ways to wear\n\ndrawstring waist / adjustable waist\n\ndetachable belt / adjustable belt\n\nSnap-front abaya with flap + s", "source": "market/D2_Functional_Structure_Preferences_TextCorpus.docx", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-D3_Sizing_BodyFit_Pr-001", "title": "Sizing & Body-Fit Preferences (D3)", "content": "Sizing & Body-Fit Preferences (D3)\n\nText corpus: size chart writing patterns, return-reason attribution, and optimization suggestions (data-oriented).\n\n尺码偏移的典型“误解点”：同样标 S/M/L 或同样标 54/56/58，不同品牌宽松度与衣长策略不一致，导致“买对长度却买错宽度”。\n\n在中东/GCC 常见的 abaya 尺码逻辑是“按衣长（英寸）定码”，例如 54=衣长 54 英寸（从肩点到下摆），并非传统欧美的胸围/腰围主导。\n\n偏大/偏小通常来自两个维度：①衣长（对身高/鞋跟敏感）②宽松量（对胸/臀围与“是否贴身”敏感）。\n\n写法一（长度主导）：Size number = garment length (inches). Height → recommended size.\n\n写法二（双表并列）：表 A 写身高→建议尺码；表 B 写同尺码的衣身宽度（胸围/臀围/下摆围）与袖长。\n\n写法三（用例说明）：用一个具体人物示例解释“介于两档身高”“穿高跟”“想更拖地/更到脚踝”的选择差异。\n\n脚踝长度（更适合日常）：下摆覆盖脚踝但不拖地；楼梯、通勤更安全。\n\n贴地/拖地（更适合场合）：用于 Eid、晚宴、婚礼等更正式的垂坠感；室外更", "source": "market/D3_Sizing_BodyFit_Preferences_TextCorpus.docx", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-D3_Sizing_BodyFit_Pr-002", "title": "Length = shoulder-to-hem (inches). 尺码数字就是衣长（英寸）。", "content": "Length = shoulder-to-hem (inches). 尺码数字就是衣长（英寸）。\n\n如何测量：从肩点（肩颈交界最高点）量到你想要的下摆位置（脚踝/贴地）。\n\n介于两档：想更端庄/穿跟 → 选长一档；想更日常/不拖地 → 选短一档。\n\n退货原因一级分类建议：①长度不合适 ②宽松度不合适（偏大/偏小）③期望不符（材质/厚薄/透明度）④色差 ⑤瑕疵/做工 ⑥其他。\n\n二级原因细分（用于改版）：长度过长/过短；胸围偏紧/偏松；袖长偏短/偏长；肩部过窄/过宽；下摆围影响走路；穿跟后露脚踝。\n\n线上服装退货率在多个研究/行业文章中常被引用为 20–30% 的量级（不同市场与品类波动较大）。\n\n尺码/合身问题是服装线上退货的高频原因；部分行业文章给出“尺码导致退货占比 30–40%（在服装退货中）”的估计口径。\n\n把“身高→衣长”做成首屏选择器：先选身高段，再选想要脚踝/贴地，再给出建议尺码与试穿效果图。\n\n把“成衣胸围/臀围”公开：让用户知道同一码的宽松度，减少“买大了/买小了”的主观误差。\n\n在商品页增加 3 个固定字段：Model height、Model size、Heel height（平底/高跟），统一口径。\n\n对高退货 SKU 做“尺码注释标签”：Runs long / Runs short / Extra loose / Narrow shoulders。\n\n把退", "source": "market/D3_Sizing_BodyFit_Preferences_TextCorpus.docx", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-D3_Sizing_BodyFit_Pr-003", "title": "Height-based sizing + size up for heels + modest fit ease: https://www.shamswear", "content": "Height-based sizing + size up for heels + modest fit ease: https://www.shamswear.com/pages/size-guide\n\nOpen abaya height/bust/length table: https://fajrnoor.com/pages/open-abaya-size-chart\n\nOnline return rate (20-30%) benchmark: https://www.beumergroup.com/knowledge/wd/handling-the-challenges-of-returns-in-the-e-commerce-fashion-industry/\n\nSizing issues share of returns (industry estimate): https://www.fitezapp.com/blog/reduce-fashion-returns.html", "source": "market/D3_Sizing_BodyFit_Preferences_TextCorpus.docx", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
