    {"id": "MARKET-Knight_Frank_Industr-001", "title": "Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 20241", "content": "Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 20241\nSaudi Arabia Industrial \nAnd Logistics Market \nReview\nH1 2024 A biannual review of key trends and the performance of \nSaudi Arabia’s industrial and logistics market  knightfrank.com.sa/en/research", "source": "market/Knight_Frank_Industrial_Logistics_H1_2024.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Knight_Frank_Industr-002", "title": "Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 2024 Saudi Arabia Indus", "content": "Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 2024 Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 20242 3\nAN INDUSTRIAL POWERHOUSE\nSaudi Arabia’s industrial sector has experienced significant \ngrowth in recent years, driven by strategic initiatives, \ntechnological advancements, and substantial investments, \nall of which have positioned the Kingdom as a burgeoning \nindustrial hub in the Middle East.\nIn 2023, inflation-adjusted non-oil economic activity in Saudi \nArabia grew by 3.8% over 2022. Non-oil economic output \ntotalled SAR 2.5 trillion (US$ 672 billion), accounting f", "source": "market/Knight_Frank_Industrial_Logistics_H1_2024.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Knight_Frank_Industr-003", "title": "Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 2024 Saudi Arabia Indus", "content": "Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 2024 Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 20244 5NUMBERS YOU NEED TO \nKNOW\n410SAR 557 bn\n505\n2.1 million \nSAR 38.6 bn \nSAR 9 7. 5 bn 11,434 \nSAR 895 bn83.7%\nSAR 892 bn 8.3%\n8.0%Number of new industrial licenses \nissued during Jan to April 2024Saudi Arabia’s industrial sector growth Saudi Arabia’s national industrial strategy targets for 2030\nAnnual industrial exports by 2030\nNumber of factories that began \nproduction during Jan to April 2024\nNew jobs by 2030\nTotal capital of new licensed factories \nduring Jan to April", "source": "market/Knight_Frank_Industrial_Logistics_H1_2024.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Knight_Frank_Industr-004", "title": "Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 2024 Saudi Arabia Indus", "content": "Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 2024 Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 20246 7SAUDI BUILDING CODE\nThe Saudi Building Code, aligned with MOMRA, has established \nregulations and standards for warehouses in warehouse \ndistricts. These warehouses have been classified into three main \ncategories: Low Hazard (S1), which includes plastic warehouses; Medium Hazard (S2), which includes construction materials; \nand High Hazard (H), which includes flammable materials. \nHowever, it should be noted that the guidelines do not cover \nclass H warehouses.\nMODON\nM", "source": "market/Knight_Frank_Industrial_Logistics_H1_2024.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Knight_Frank_Industr-005", "title": "Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 2024 Saudi Arabia Indus", "content": "Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 2024 Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 20248 9SURGE IN DEMAND\nAcross the Kingdom, there continues to be a notable surge in the \ndemand for warehouse facilities, with Riyadh emerging as the \nepicenter of demand. This surge can be attributed to a variety \nof factors, including the booming e-commerce sector, the rapid \nmaterialisation of the Kingdom’s giga projects and the wide-\nspread adoption of cutting-edge technologies like robotics.\nGIGA PROJECTS BOOSTING DEMAND IN RIYADH\nAlong with ongoing transportation and inf", "source": "market/Knight_Frank_Industrial_Logistics_H1_2024.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Knight_Frank_Industr-006", "title": "Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 2024 Saudi Arabia Indus", "content": "Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 2024 Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 202410 11SUPPLY CONTINUES TO GROW\nMirroring the trend in Riyadh, Jeddah’s industrial and logistics \nsector has also seen a significant increase in supply over the past \n12 months, bringing the total warehouse and logistics facility \nstock to 19.6 million sqm. \nJeddah has also seen large-scale developments, bringing the \ntotal warehouse and logistics facilities stock to 19.6 million \nsqm, with notable projects including Maersk’s logistics park \nand Aramex’s warehouse in Jeddah ", "source": "market/Knight_Frank_Industrial_Logistics_H1_2024.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Knight_Frank_Industr-007", "title": "Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 2024 Saudi Arabia Indus", "content": "Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 2024 Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 202412 13\nA KEY LOGISTICS HUB FOR THE KINGDOM\nThe industrial and logistics sector is poised for continued growth \nin DMA, driven by strategic infrastructure investments, the rise of \ne-commerce, and the region’s critical role in Saudi Arabia’s economic \ndiversification efforts. \nThe modernisation of facilities and the increasing demand for high-\nquality warehouses are likely to attract further investments, making \nthe Eastern Province a key logistics hub in the Kingdom. \nFor i", "source": "market/Knight_Frank_Industrial_Logistics_H1_2024.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Knight_Frank_Industr-008", "title": "Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 2024 Saudi Arabia Indus", "content": "Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 2024 Saudi Arabia Industrial And Logistics Market Review   H1 202414 15THE OPPORTUNITY IN SAUDI ARABIA ’S INDUSTRIAL MARKET\nSUPPLY SHORTAGE\nSaudi Arabia is currently facing a shortage of warehousing, a \nsituation exacerbated by the cautious investment behavior of \nlandowners. Many are hesitant to develop speculatively due \nto their lack of experience in creating a real estate that meets \ninternational standards. This caution is understandable, \ngiven the complexities involved in constructing high-quality \nwarehouse facilities that align ", "source": "market/Knight_Frank_Industrial_Logistics_H1_2024.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Knight_Frank_Industr-009", "title": "@MENAKnightFrank @KnightFrankMENA @KnightFrankUAE", "content": "@MENAKnightFrank @KnightFrankMENA @KnightFrankUAE\n@KnightFrankMENA @KnightFrankMENACONTACTS\nSUSAN AMAWI\nGeneral Manager, KSA\nsusan.amawi@me.knightfrank.com\nADAM WYNNE, MRICS\nPartner - Occupier/Landlord Strategy & Solutions \nadam.wynne@me.knightfrank.com\nMIKHAIL VERESHCHAGIN \nAssociate Partner - Industrial & Logistics, KSA\nmikhail.vereshchagin@me.knightfrank.comTALAL RAQABAN, MRICS\nPartner - Head of Valuation and Advisory, KSA\ntalal.raqaban@me.knightfrank.comANDREW LOVE\nRegional Partner - Head of Capital Markets & Occupier/ Landlord \nStrategy and Solutions, MENA\nandrew.love@me.knightfrank.comMO", "source": "market/Knight_Frank_Industrial_Logistics_H1_2024.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
