    {"id": "MARKET-Knight_Frank_Retail_-004", "title": "Saudi Arabia Retail Market Overview Saudi Arabia Retail Market Overview6 7", "content": "Saudi Arabia Retail Market Overview Saudi Arabia Retail Market Overview6 7\nJeddah\nRed Sea Mall\nRISING SUPPLY \nIn the past 10 months, Jeddah’s retail market has seen an influx \nof diverse and vibrant retail offerings, adding approximately \n175,000 sqm of new space. This growth includes the addition of \nseveral zones at Souq 7 which, along with other developments \nsuch as La Paz (13,500 sqm), have added approximately 175,000 \nsqm of new space, bringing the total retail supply in Jeddah \nto 2.83 million sqm. This expansion includes a mix of high-\nend boutiques, contemporary brands, and unique loc", "source": "market/Knight_Frank_Retail_Overview_Autumn_2024.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Knight_Frank_Retail_-005", "title": "Saudi Arabia Retail Market Overview Saudi Arabia Retail Market Overview8 9", "content": "Saudi Arabia Retail Market Overview Saudi Arabia Retail Market Overview8 9\nMarket wide occupancy rates - Q3 2024\nSource: Knight FrankQ3 20230 PP\nY/ YQ3 2024Occupancy Vacancy\n10% 10%\n90%90%Dammam Metropolitan \nArea (DMA)\nSTABLE OCCUPANCY LEVELS\nIn DMA, demand from retailers for space in regional and super-\nregional malls remains strong, with occupancy rates holding \nsteady at 90%. However, rental rates have experienced a slight \ndip over the past year, declining by 0.7% to an average of SAR \n2,285 psm. \nThis modest decrease in rental rates suggests a slight softening \nin the market, even as dem", "source": "market/Knight_Frank_Retail_Overview_Autumn_2024.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
