    {"id": "MARKET-Saudi_Arabia_Report_-022", "title": "28", "content": "28\nConclusion \nBrands know the consumer appetite for AR is already here – consumers are far more likely to pay attention to brands using AR. There is a content imperative for brands to meet consumers AR demand, and now is the time to meet this demand. Brands that meet the demand for AR experiences may be more likely to gain market share in the future.  Consumers continuously expect more personalized and engaging experiences that enable them to interact with  the world. AR is delivering that to consumers, today, but there remains untapped potential for so much more. The convergence of use cases", "source": "market/Saudi_Arabia_Report_Snap_Consumer_AR.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Saudi_Arabia_Report_-023", "title": "Consumers are  redefining the digital experience by using AR.Augmented Reality (", "content": "Consumers are  redefining the digital experience by using AR.Augmented Reality (AR) is the next form of mobile engagement that is exciting consumers, driving an enhanced engagement with brands, elevating consumer experiences and increasing brand revenues.31Augmented Reality refers to experiences in which the real-world environment seen through your phone, computer, app camera, or an AR headset is altered or enhanced with the addition of images, objects, text, or other digitally-added information. Augmented Reality could be applied to both visuals of the front facing (selfie) and outward facing", "source": "market/Saudi_Arabia_Report_Snap_Consumer_AR.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Saudi_Arabia_Report_-024", "title": "32Research Overview  Saudi Arabia Report, Quantitative Online Survey •20-minute ", "content": "32Research Overview  Saudi Arabia Report, Quantitative Online Survey •20-minute online survey among 15,000 international respondents •Survey in field from February 23, 2021 – April 5, 2021 Alignment with  Interdisciplinary Experts •Experts within the AR industry participated in in-depth interviews to provide context for survey findings and contribute guidance on the future of AR in society.Respondent Qualification •n=1000 per market •Ages 13-50 •500 Snapchatters who use Snapchat at least once daily, split evenly amongst age groups 13-17, 18-24, and 25-50 •To ensure a representative read on Sna", "source": "market/Saudi_Arabia_Report_Snap_Consumer_AR.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
