    {"id": "MARKET-Snap_Consumer_AR_Res-002", "title": "AR is a critical tool for brands to capture consumer attention, better connect w", "content": "AR is a critical tool for brands to capture consumer attention, better connect with people, and build consumer confidence.IntroductionTable of  Contents\n20102AR’s Impact on BrandsAR is Evolving Fast AR is Here Today and Here to StayConclusion030406AR is evolving at a rapid rate and is poised to take-oﬀ and become as significant of a technology shift as the web or mobile. \nThe camera is driving the adoption of AR from being a playful technology to being a ubiquitous experience that drives excitement and utility into people’s lives.AR is already here, widely recognized as both fun  and useful, a", "source": "market/Snap_Consumer_AR_Research_GlobalReport.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Snap_Consumer_AR_Res-003", "title": "1: See additional methodology details in appendix 2: 2021 Global Deloitte Digita", "content": "1: See additional methodology details in appendix 2: 2021 Global Deloitte Digital Study commissioned by Snap Inc. Base = Aggregate average (n=11,457) Q: AR Recognition for 9 examples 3: Base = Aggregate (n=10,166) Q: Why do you use AR? 4: Base = Aggregate (n=11,938) Q: Augmented Reality is useful / Augmented Reality is not useful | A: Agree much more with A, Agree somewhat more with A5: Harvard Business Review Article, “How AR is Redefining Retail in the Pandemic”65% of AR consumers around the world and across generations use AR to have fun; the majority are discovering AR through social / com", "source": "market/Snap_Consumer_AR_Research_GlobalReport.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Snap_Consumer_AR_Res-004", "title": "Consumers are  redefining the digital experience by using AR. Augmented Reality ", "content": "Consumers are  redefining the digital experience by using AR. Augmented Reality (AR) is the next form of mobile engagement that is exciting consumers, driving an enhanced engagement with brands, elevating consumer experiences and increasing brand revenues.5Augmented Reality refers to experiences in which the real-world environment seen through your phone, computer, app camera, or an AR headset is altered or enhanced with the addition of images, objects, text, or other digitally-added information. Augmented Reality could be applied to both visuals of the front facing (selfie) and outward facing", "source": "market/Snap_Consumer_AR_Research_GlobalReport.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Snap_Consumer_AR_Res-005", "title": "There is something really unique happening right now – an incredible number of h", "content": "There is something really unique happening right now – an incredible number of hobbyists and professionals are using AR. Downloading tools across the Snap AR platform. They’re taking time to learn, they’re curious.” Eitan Pilipski  SVP Camera Platform Snap Inc. 6\nAR is growing By 2025, nearly 75% of the global population* and almost all people who use social / communication apps will be frequent AR users.1\n1.5B2.2B 2.9B3.5B \n2021 2022 2023 2024 2025 Gen Z Millennial Gen X 4.3B \n0.0B0.5B1.0B1.5B2.0B2.5B3.0B4.0BBoomer 3.5BFrequent AR ConsumersBased on people ages 13-69 who use social / communica", "source": "market/Snap_Consumer_AR_Research_GlobalReport.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Snap_Consumer_AR_Res-006", "title": "7", "content": "7\nEvan Spiegel Chief Executive Officer Snap Inc.  \nSnap Inc. Q4 2020 Earning\'s CallOur commitment to reinventing the camera is most evident through our advances in augmented reality. Today, more than 200 million people engage with AR on Snapchat everyday on average. We have co-developed our vision for augmented reality together with our growing community and have created cutting-edged tools and capabilities that allow creators to build increasingly advanced Lenses and distribute them to the entire Snapchat community.”", "source": "market/Snap_Consumer_AR_Research_GlobalReport.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Snap_Consumer_AR_Res-007", "title": "vYounger,  more group- oriented households are driving  AR growth Age Difference", "content": "vYounger,  more group- oriented households are driving  AR growth Age DifferencesHousehold\nBigger households are 89% more likely than solo households to use AR all the time.3\nNote: People who live with others is based on households with 5 or more individuals. Increased number of household members implies more time spent being social with friends and family, a driver of AR usage.Gen Z / Millennials are both 71% more likely to use AR all the time  vs. older generations.1  Older generations are nearly  20% more likely to view AR primarily as practical.2 \n1: 2021 Global Deloitte Digital Study comm", "source": "market/Snap_Consumer_AR_Research_GlobalReport.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Snap_Consumer_AR_Res-008", "title": "Compared to mobile tech adoption AR is poised  to take-off 9Technology    advanc", "content": "Compared to mobile tech adoption AR is poised  to take-off 9Technology    advances are   driving the    accelerated    adoption of AR:AR-related patents in the US grew more than 3x over the last 10 years.15G will accelerate AR technology adoption with benefits like increased download speeds and accessibility.22000 0%10%20%30%40%50%60%70%90%80%100%\n2001 2002 2003 2004 2005 2006 2007 2008 2009 2010 2011 2012 2013 2014 2015 2021 2025 AR Equivalent Dates:2022 2023 2024 \nAR Adoption Rate TodayAR Adoption Rate 2025AR is tracking with the mobile usage boom \n5G\n1: Deloitte Digital Insights, The Spatia", "source": "market/Snap_Consumer_AR_Research_GlobalReport.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Snap_Consumer_AR_Res-009", "title": "As AR evolves, it will revolutionize our lives and will become as  significant o", "content": "As AR evolves, it will revolutionize our lives and will become as  significant of a technology shift as the web or mobile was to society, changing how we view and interact with the world around us.” 10\nAllan Cook Digital Reality Business Leader Deloitte Digital\n\nconsumers94%A lot of people are using AR to make purchase decisions and plan to keep doing so \n12There are100 millionagree they\'ll use AR the same or  more when shopping next year.2shopping with AR online  and in-stores.1\n1: Gartner Press Release 2: 2021 Global Deloitte Digital Study commissioned by Snap Inc.  Base = Aggregate (n=6,878", "source": "market/Snap_Consumer_AR_Research_GlobalReport.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Snap_Consumer_AR_Res-010", "title": "AR is the new  consumer  experience  and cannot  be ignored$", "content": "AR is the new  consumer  experience  and cannot  be ignored$\nPCWebMobileCompanies that Adopted, Banked\nCompanies that Didn’t, SankAREvolution of Consumer ExperienceConsumers continuously expect more personalized and engaging experiences that enable them to interact with the world. The companies that embrace change can become dominant industry players – those that don’t, fall behind competitors …and sink. It’s not too late to be a leader and get first mover benefits.13", "source": "market/Snap_Consumer_AR_Research_GlobalReport.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Snap_Consumer_AR_Res-011", "title": "Andrew McPhee  Design Innovation  Snap Inc.14", "content": "Andrew McPhee  Design Innovation  Snap Inc.14\nHistorically, advertising interrupted your  life to get your attention. With AR a brand  can create content that you can personalize with the camera and leverage to tell your  own story in a way that is genuinely interesting, entertaining and relevant to  your friends and followers.”", "source": "market/Snap_Consumer_AR_Research_GlobalReport.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Snap_Consumer_AR_Res-012", "title": "AR captures consumer  attention", "content": "AR captures consumer  attention\nPeople who frequently  use AR with their family and friends are 50% more likely to pay attention to  a brand.2 leading to improved memories and more powerful responses from consumers.1AR delivers almost  2x the levels of visual attention compared to their non-AR equivalent, AR\n1: Zappar Article, “How augmented reality aﬀects the brain” 2: 2021 Global Deloitte Digital Study commissioned by Snap Inc. Base = Over 60% of friends and family sharing AR (n=1,330), Less than 20% of friends and family sharing AR (n=1,209) Q: How many of your friends and family do you thi", "source": "market/Snap_Consumer_AR_Research_GlobalReport.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Snap_Consumer_AR_Res-013", "title": "Brands and people connect better with AR experiences41% Brands are ", "content": "Brands and people connect better with AR experiences41% Brands are \n1: 2021 Global Deloitte Digital Study commissioned by Snap Inc.  Base = People who use AR all the time (n=1,760) Q: Sometimes brands will create AR experiences through an app camera (e.g., a big movie company makes an AR experience where the heroes of a movie are fighting next to you, or a restaurant provides you a lens/filter/eﬀect that turns you into a hamburger). What impact, if any, does interacting with that AR experience have on your perception of that brand? | A: I am more likely to pay more attention to the brand, I am", "source": "market/Snap_Consumer_AR_Research_GlobalReport.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Snap_Consumer_AR_Res-014", "title": "AR builds consumer confidence ", "content": "AR builds consumer confidence \n17of shoppers agree  that AR gives them more confidence  about product quality.1 +of people want to use AR technology to assess products, allowing for a risk free, “try-before you buy”, experience.2Nearly 3 in 4 consumers  say they\'re willing to pay more for  a product that promises the total transparency that AR can provide.356% \n1: 2021 Global Deloitte Digital Study commissioned by Snap Inc. Base = Aggregate (n=8,770)Q: How does AR impact your browsing and/or shopping experience?2: NielsenIQ Analysis, Augmented retail: The new consumer reality3: 2016 Label Insi", "source": "market/Snap_Consumer_AR_Research_GlobalReport.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Snap_Consumer_AR_Res-015", "title": "Social is driving AR adoption. People want to share their  favorite Brand’s  AR ", "content": "Social is driving AR adoption. People want to share their  favorite Brand’s  AR experiences 18\nNote: Letters indicate statistically significant diﬀerence at 95% confidence levelRely on friends and family to discover branded AR experiences1Gen Z Millennials Gen X 33%35%39%\n1:  2021 Alter Agents research commissioned by Snap Inc. and Publicis MediaGen Z Millennials Gen X 54%64%63%Find it important to share branded AR easily1", "source": "market/Snap_Consumer_AR_Research_GlobalReport.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Snap_Consumer_AR_Res-016", "title": "The conversion rates that we’ve seen have surprised us, as a result we’re doubli", "content": "The conversion rates that we’ve seen have surprised us, as a result we’re doubling-down  on AR experiences to drive eCommerce.”\n94% \n20higher conversion rate, as individuals can better assess them and feel connected with brands.1AR interactions drive conversion\nRobert Triefus EVP of Brand & Customer Engagement  Gucci\nInteracting with products that have AR experiences leads to a\nVS.1: Harvard Business Review Article, “How AR is Redefining Retail in the Pandemic”", "source": "market/Snap_Consumer_AR_Research_GlobalReport.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
