    {"id": "MARKET-Snap_Consumer_AR_Res-018", "title": "As mobile devices improve, the phone and the camera are becoming synonymous, all", "content": "As mobile devices improve, the phone and the camera are becoming synonymous, allowing everyone to experience  the world through each others’ eyes. Today, we experience the world through the lens of the camera… Consumers are 23% more likely to use the front-facing camera when  they use AR to express themselves.1 …tomorrow, the lens will become smart glasses. The camera will… Be the New Search  Pointing your camera at something will be similar to typing a term into a search bar. \n“Snap’s choice of a smartphone’s camera as the interface is a familiar, comfortable tool that is almost always within", "source": "market/Snap_Consumer_AR_Research_GlobalReport.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Snap_Consumer_AR_Res-019", "title": "In tech, there is an inner circle  (now-18 months) and outer circle (18-36 month", "content": "In tech, there is an inner circle  (now-18 months) and outer circle (18-36 months)  of trends to take seriously. AR is properly in  the inner circle. Nothing is more powerful than  AR; it is the bridge between the 2D and the 3D world, and we’ve never had that before – we instead forced ourselves to accept the 2D world that you cannot touch or live.”24\nPaul McDonagh-Smith Digital Capability Leader Massachusetts Institute of Technology", "source": "market/Snap_Consumer_AR_Research_GlobalReport.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-Snap_Consumer_AR_Res-020", "title": "Experiment with  interesting features.", "content": "Experiment with  interesting features.\nUnderstand the benefits or utility of AR experiences. As this understanding grows, so too, do practical applications and how they might be used.          Discover and test  a new capability.\nInteract with frictionless applications and experiences. Expectations to use AR becomes ubiquitous across platforms, providing interaction points to engage with the world in its totality. \nWE ARE HERE 25E.G. Trying out a brand’s lipstick to see how it  looks on or how a TV looks on the wall to determine which size of TV to purchase.E.G. Testing out a hair color and sh", "source": "market/Snap_Consumer_AR_Research_GlobalReport.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
