    {"id": "MARKET-report_trdev_jun21_e-050", "title": "- 50 - ", "content": "- 50 - \n  \n  3.102.   In total, 11 G20 economies (counting the Europea n Union as one) received 110 questions \non 61 SIMs under Article 18.6 at the 96th and 97th CoA meetings.  As shown in Chart 3.21, the \nannual average number of questions raised under Article 18.6 concerning G20 members\' policies \nhas been on the rise since 2011, reaching an all -time high of an average of 61 questions per \nmeeting in 2020. These numbers include questions that were repeated in more than one meeting.   \nChart 3.21 Average number of questions posed to G20  economies on SIMs under Article \n18.6 (1995-2021a) \n \n", "source": "market/report_trdev_jun21_e.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-sa044ar-001", "title": "اﻟﻤﻠﻜﻲ  اﻟﻤﺮﺳﻮم  ﺑﻤﻮﺟﺐ  اﻟﺴﻌﻮدي  اﻟﺘﺠﺎرﻳﺔ  اﻟﻮآﺎﻻت  ﻧﻈﺎم   ", "content": "اﻟﻤﻠﻜﻲ  اﻟﻤﺮﺳﻮم  ﺑﻤﻮﺟﺐ  اﻟﺴﻌﻮدي  اﻟﺘﺠﺎرﻳﺔ  اﻟﻮآﺎﻻت  ﻧﻈﺎم   \n رﻗﻢ11  ﺗﺎرﻳﺦ 22/ 7 / 1962  \n ﺗﻌﺎﻟﻰ اﷲ ﺑﻌﻮن   \nاﻟﻤﻠﻚ ﺟﻼﻟﺔ  ﺑﺄﺳﻢ   \n  \nﺳﻌﻮد ﺁل اﻟﻌﺰﻳﺰ  ﻋﺒﺪ ﺑﻦ ﻓﻴﺼﻞ  ﻧﺤﻦ   \nاﻟﺴﻌﻮدﻳﺔ  اﻟﻌﺮﺑﻴﺔ اﻟﻤﻤﻠﻜﺔ  ﻣﻠﻚ ﺟﻼﻟﺔ  ﻧﺎﺋﺐ   \n  \nا ﺑﺎﻟﻤﺮﺳﻮم اﻟﺼﺎدر  اﻟﻮزراء  \nﻣﺠﻠﺲ ﻧﻈﺎم  ﻣﻦ ﻋﺸﺮ اﻟﺘﺎﺳﻌﺔ اﻟﻤﺎدة  ﻋﻠﻰ اﻻﻃﻼع ﺑﻌﺪ  رﻗﻢ ﻟﻤﻠﻜﻲ 28  وﺗﺎرﻳﺦ \n22 / 10 / 1377 هـ  . \n رﻗﻢ اﻟﻮزراء  ﻣﺠﻠﺲ ﻗﺮار  ﻋﻠﻰ وﺑﻨﺎء 86وﺗﺎرﻳﺦ  12 / 2 / 1382 هـ  .\nاﻟﻮزراء  ﻣﺠﻠﺲ رﺋﻴﺲ  ﻋﻠﻴﻨﺎ ﻋﺮﺿﻪ  ﻣﺎ ﻋﻠﻰ  وﺑﻨﺎء  . \n  \n ﺁت هﻮ ﺑﻤﺎ ﻧﺮﺳﻢ  : \n  \n اوﻻ-ﻟﻬﺬا  اﻟﻤﺮاﻓﻘﺔ  ﺑﺎﻟﺼﻴﻐﺔ اﻟﺘﺠﺎرﻳﺔ  اﻟﻮآﺎﻻت ﻧﻈﺎم  ﻋﻠﻰ ﻧﺼﺎدق  . \n ﺛﺎﻧﻴﺎ-اﻟﺘﺠﺎر  ووزﻳﺮ  اﻟﻮزراء  ﻣﺠﻠﺲ رﺋﻴﺲ  ﻋﻠﻰ هﺬا ﻣﺮﺳﻮﻣﻨ", "source": "market/sa044ar.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-sa044ar-002", "title": "اﻟﻤﺎدة4  ", "content": "اﻟﻤﺎدة4  \n) م رﻗﻢ اﻟﻤﻠﻜﻲ  ﺑﺎﻟﻤﺮﺳﻮم ﻋﺪﻟﺖ  آﻤﺎ/ 32  ﺗﺎرﻳﺦ 1400 / 8 / 10 هـ (  وﻻﺋﺤﺘﻪ  اﻟﻨﻈﺎم  هﺬا اﺣﻜﺎم  ﻳﺨﺎﻟﻒ ﻣﻦ  آﻞ\n ﻧﻔﻘﺔ ﻋﻠﻰ اﻟﻌﻘﻮﺑﺔ  ﻧﺸﺮ ﻣﻊ رﻳﺎل اﻟﻒ ﺧﻤﺴﻴﻦ  ﺗﺘﺠﺎوز  وﻻ رﻳﺎل اﻻف ﺧﻤﺴﺔ  ﻋﻦ ﺗﻘﻞ ﻻ  ﺑﻐﺮاﻣﺔ  ﻳﻌﺎﻗﺐ اﻟﺘﻨﻔﻴﺬﻳﺔ\nﻟﺤﻘﻪ ﻣﻦ  ﺑﺤﻖ اﺧﻼل  دون وذﻟﻚ ﺑﺎﻟﺘﻌﻮﻳﺾاﻟﻤﺨﺎﻟﻒ  اﻟﻤﻄﺎﻟﺒﺔ ﻓﻲ  اﻟﻤﺨﺎﻟﻔﺔ  ﻣﻦ ﺿﺮر .  اﻟﻤﺨﺎﻟﻔﺔ  آﺎﻧﺖ ﻓﺎن\n اﻟﻐﺮاﻣﺔ  اﻟﻰ ﺑﺎﻻﺿﺎﻓﺔ اﻟﻌﻘﻮﺑﺔ أﺻﺒﺤﺖ  ﺳﻌﻮدي  ﻏﻴﺮ أآﺜﺮ أو ﺷﺮﻳﻚ ﻓﻴﻬﺎ  ﺳﻌﻮدﻳﺔ  ﻟﺸﺮآﺔ أو ﻷﺟﻨﺒﻲ  ﻣﻨﺴﻮﺑﺔ\n اﻻﻣﺮ اﻟﺪاﺧﻠﻴﺔ  ﻟﻮزﻳﺮ وﻳﺠﻮز ﻣﻌﻴﻨﺔ  ﻟﻤﺪة او داﺋﻤﺎ اﻟﺘﺠﺎرة  ﻣﻤﺎرﺳﺔ  ﻣﻦ اﻟﺤﺮﻣﺎن  ﺟﻮاز ﻣﻊ ادارﻳﺎ  اﻻﻋﻤﺎل  ﺗﺼﻔﻴﺔ\nﺑﺘﺮﺣ  اﻟﺸﺮﻳﻚ  او اﻻﺟﻨﺒﻲ  ﻋﻦ\n اﺑﻼﻏﻪ  اﻟﺘﺠﺎرة  وزارة  وﻋﻠﻰ  ﺑﻬﺎ اﻟﻤﺤﻜﻮم اﻟﻌﻘﻮﺑﺔ ﺿ", "source": "market/sa044ar.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-sa044ar-003", "title": "3 اﻟﻤﺎدة10  ", "content": "3 اﻟﻤﺎدة10  \n) م رﻗﻢ اﻟﻤﻠﻜﻲ  ﺑﺎﻟﻤﺮﺳﻮم اﺿﻴﻔﺖ  آﻤﺎ/ 5  ﺗﺎرﻳﺦ 1389 / 6 / 11 هـ (  وزﻳﺮ اﻣﺎم اﻟﻬﻴﺌﺔ هﺬﻩ ﻗﺮارات  ﻣﻦ اﻟﺘﻈﻠﻢ  ﻳﺠﻮز\n ﻗﺮاراﺗﻬﺎ  اﺻﺒﺤﺖ  واﻻ ، ﻋﻨﻪ ﻳﻨﻮب  ﻣﻦ او ﻟﻠﻤﺘﻈﻠﻢ  اﺑﻼﻏﻬﺎ ﻣﻦ  ﻳﻮﻣﺎ ﻋﺸﺮ ﺧﻤﺴﺔ  ﺧﻼل ﻓﻲ واﻟﺼﻨﺎﻋﺔ  اﻟﺘﺠﺎرة\nوﺗ اﻟﻤﺬآﻮرة  اﻟﻤﺪة ﺑﻤﻀﻲ  ﻋﻠﻴﻬﺎﻧﻬﺎﺋﻴﺔ  واﻟﺼﻨﺎﻋﺔ  اﻟﺘﺠﺎرة  وزﻳﺮ ﺼﺪﻳﻖ.     \n اﻟﻤﺎدة11  \n) م رﻗﻢ اﻟﻤﻠﻜﻲ  ﺑﺎﻟﻤﺮﺳﻮم ﻋﺪﻟﺖ  آﻤﺎ/ 8  ﺗﺎرﻳﺦ 1393/ 3 / 20هـ (  آﺎﻻﺗﻲ  اﻟﻮآﺎﻻت ﺳﺠﻞ  ﻓﻲ اﻟﻘﻴﺪ رﺳﻮم  ﺗﺤﺪد:  \nاﻟﺸﺮآﺔ  او اﻟﻔﺮد ﻟﻠﺘﺎﺟﺮ  رﻳﺎﻻ ﺧﻤﺴﻤﺎﻳﺔ.  واﺣﺪة ﻟﻤﺮة اﻟﺮﺳﻮم  وﺗﺪﻓﻊ.     \n اﻟﻤﺎدة12  \nﺗﺎرﻳﺦ ﻣﻦ اﺷﻬﺮ  ﺛﻼﺛﺔ ﺑﻌﺪ اﻟﻨﻈﺎم ﺑﻬﺬا ﻧﺸﺮﻩﻳﻌﻤﻞ    .", "source": "market/sa044ar.pdf", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-the_influence_of_med-001", "title": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  ", "content": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  \nVol. 14, No. 6, 2024, E-ISSN:  2222 -6990 © 2024  \n \n906 \n The Influence of Media on the Trend of Saudi \nWomen towards Purchasing Traditional Clothing  \n \nMaha Bint Abdullah Aldabbagh  \nProfessor of Fashion Marketing King Abdulaziz University Saudi Arabia  \nAbstract  \nThis study aims to assess the current trends among Saudi women towards purchasing \ntraditional fashions,  examine the influence of various forms of media, including social media \nplatforms, television, print media, and online fashion blogs, on the desire", "source": "market/the-influence-of-media-on-the-trend-of-saudi-women-towards-purchasing-traditional-clothing.pd", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-the_influence_of_med-002", "title": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  ", "content": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  \nVol. 14, No. 6, 2024, E-ISSN:  2222 -6990 © 2024  \n \n907 \n bags and shoes (Lee et al., 2009). The environment, geographical location, customs and \nreligious and historical values also play a significant role in the forms, materials and methods \nof making each of them (Abdul Moneim, 2010).  \nThe Kingdom has a rich heritage of distinctive cultural fashions, with styles of dress \nvarying between women and men in different regions. Saudi cultural dress is characterized by \ndifferent fabrics such as silk, cotton, gold wire", "source": "market/the-influence-of-media-on-the-trend-of-saudi-women-towards-purchasing-traditional-clothing.pd", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-the_influence_of_med-003", "title": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  ", "content": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  \nVol. 14, No. 6, 2024, E-ISSN:  2222 -6990 © 2024  \n \n908 \n and media influence, stakeholders can devise strategies to foster a more inclusive, culturally \nresonant fashion landscape that celebrates Saudi heritage while embracing the possibilities of \nthe digital age.  \n \nResearch Problem  \nThe trend of Saudi women towards purchasing traditional fashions and the influence of the \nmedia on their desire to buy them represent complex and multifaceted phenomena within \nthe cultural and consumer landscape of Saudi Arabia. W", "source": "market/the-influence-of-media-on-the-trend-of-saudi-women-towards-purchasing-traditional-clothing.pd", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-the_influence_of_med-004", "title": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  ", "content": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  \nVol. 14, No. 6, 2024, E-ISSN:  2222 -6990 © 2024  \n \n909 \n • To propose actionable recommendations for fashion industry stakeholders, policymakers, \nand cultural influencers to leverage media platforms effectively in promoting traditional Saudi \nfashion while respecting cultural sensitivities and preserving authenticity.  \n \nResearch Hypotheses  \n1- There are statistically significant differences in the direction of Saudi women towards \nacquiring traditional clothing based on demographic variables.  \n2- There are stat", "source": "market/the-influence-of-media-on-the-trend-of-saudi-women-towards-purchasing-traditional-clothing.pd", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-the_influence_of_med-005", "title": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  ", "content": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  \nVol. 14, No. 6, 2024, E-ISSN:  2222 -6990 © 2024  \n \n910 \n economic changes (Khamis, 2008). Saudi women became aware of fashion trends from around \nthe world, both modern and traditional (Alsaggar, 2023)  \nFashion in the Kingdom has been influenced by several factors, including geographical, \nhistorical, customs, and traditional factors associated with clothing. This has led to its diversity \ndepending on the different regions, with each region having its own character reflected in its \ncostumes. The surrounding envir", "source": "market/the-influence-of-media-on-the-trend-of-saudi-women-towards-purchasing-traditional-clothing.pd", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-the_influence_of_med-006", "title": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  ", "content": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  \nVol. 14, No. 6, 2024, E-ISSN:  2222 -6990 © 2024  \n \n911 \n  \nFig 1: Fashion in the Northern Region  \n \nFashion in the Southern Region of Saudi Arabia  \nThe southern region of the Kingdom is also famous for its diverse traditions and atmosphere, \nand this is reflected in its traditional costumes, which are characterized by high artistic taste, \nprecision in design, and the selection of appropriate decorations (Al -Shahri, 2007). Among the \nmost prominent women\'s costumes in the southern region is (Al -Mazand), which is", "source": "market/the-influence-of-media-on-the-trend-of-saudi-women-towards-purchasing-traditional-clothing.pd", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-the_influence_of_med-007", "title": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  ", "content": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  \nVol. 14, No. 6, 2024, E-ISSN:  2222 -6990 © 2024  \n \n912 \n  \nFig2: Bani Malik dress of the south  \n \nFashion in the Eastern Region of Saudi Arabia  \nThe Eastern Region was also distinguished by the richness of its traditional costumes, \nwhich were similar to the costumes of the Najd region due to the proximity of their \ngeographical location. Its costumes were also influenced by the Indian style in fabri cs and \ndecoration style, which may be due to the deep -rooted trade between the two regions (Al -\nBassam, 2005). A", "source": "market/the-influence-of-media-on-the-trend-of-saudi-women-towards-purchasing-traditional-clothing.pd", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-the_influence_of_med-008", "title": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  ", "content": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  \nVol. 14, No. 6, 2024, E-ISSN:  2222 -6990 © 2024  \n \n913 \n  \nFig 3: Nashl dress from the fashion of the eastern region  \n \nFashion in the Western Region of Saudi Arabia  \nAs for the traditional costumes of women in the western region, they were represented \nby (Al -Zubun), which is an outer costume characterized by a princess cut and its fitting on the \nbody, and consists of a vest and pants with a tight inner dress over them, and a wide white \ndress is worn over them with embroidery around the chest, followed by an o", "source": "market/the-influence-of-media-on-the-trend-of-saudi-women-towards-purchasing-traditional-clothing.pd", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-the_influence_of_med-009", "title": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  ", "content": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  \nVol. 14, No. 6, 2024, E-ISSN:  2222 -6990 © 2024  \n \n914 \n  \nFig 4: Darfat albab dress of the western region  \n \nFifth: Fashion in the Central Region of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia:  \nFrom the western region to the central region (Najd), we find that the most prominent \nwomen’s clothing is the (maqta’) or the dir’a, which is a wide, long garment with sleeves that \nwiden from the top and gradually narrow until they reach the wrist. It has many types and \nshapes, and is embroidered with plant motifs (Fashion Authority, ", "source": "market/the-influence-of-media-on-the-trend-of-saudi-women-towards-purchasing-traditional-clothing.pd", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-the_influence_of_med-010", "title": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  ", "content": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  \nVol. 14, No. 6, 2024, E-ISSN:  2222 -6990 © 2024  \n \n915 \n  \nFig 5: Najd Almoftat dress  \n \nFashion in Saudi Arabia today  \nThe impact of Vision 2030 on Saudi Arabia\'s cultural landscape has been far -reaching, with \none of the most notable outcomes being the establishment of the Ministry of Culture in 2020. \nThis ministry plays a pivotal role in nurturing and promoting the kingdo m\'s cultural scene, both \nlocally and on the international stage. With a strong commitment to preserving the nation\'s \nhistorical heritage,", "source": "market/the-influence-of-media-on-the-trend-of-saudi-women-towards-purchasing-traditional-clothing.pd", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-the_influence_of_med-011", "title": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  ", "content": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  \nVol. 14, No. 6, 2024, E-ISSN:  2222 -6990 © 2024  \n \n916 \n immense power of mass media. As people flip through fashion magazines, tune into runway \nshows, or scroll through their Instagram feeds, they are inundated with a constant stream of \nclothing styles and trends. Over the years, mass media has played a pivotal  role in shaping \nfashion trends, and many iconic moments in fashion history can be attributed to its influence \n(Shephard et al., 2016).  \nHowever, the impact of mass media on the fashion industry is not ", "source": "market/the-influence-of-media-on-the-trend-of-saudi-women-towards-purchasing-traditional-clothing.pd", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-the_influence_of_med-012", "title": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  ", "content": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  \nVol. 14, No. 6, 2024, E-ISSN:  2222 -6990 © 2024  \n \n917 \n often emulating their fashion choices. The use of KOLs in fashion marketing has become \nincreasingly popular in recent years, with brands partnering with influencers to promote their \nproducts on social media platforms such as Instagram and TikTok. By levera ging the influence \nof KOLs, brands can quickly and effectively reach a large audience and increase their brand \nawareness (Steensma, 2015).  \nAnother way in which mass media shapes fashion trends is throu", "source": "market/the-influence-of-media-on-the-trend-of-saudi-women-towards-purchasing-traditional-clothing.pd", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
    {"id": "MARKET-the_influence_of_med-013", "title": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  ", "content": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ACADEMIC RESEARCH IN BUSINESS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES  \nVol. 14, No. 6, 2024, E-ISSN:  2222 -6990 © 2024  \n \n918 \n how media influences their choices. Participants were encouraged to respond based on their \npersonal experiences and opinions.  \n \nThe questionnaire comprised 3 axes as follows  \nAxis 1: Influence of Media on Trends and Purchasing Practices for Traditional Fashions  \nThis axis focuses on understanding the role of media in shaping Saudi women\'s awareness and \npurchasing behaviors related to traditional fashion.  \nAwareness of Advertisements:  Participants are a", "source": "market/the-influence-of-media-on-the-trend-of-saudi-women-towards-purchasing-traditional-clothing.pd", "dimension": "market", "tags": []},
